WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.360
Nice.

00:04.360 --> 00:07.320
Now we have a clear understanding what is date and time in SQL.

00:07.480 --> 00:12.600
The next question is how to manipulate those informations using SQL functions.

00:12.640 --> 00:16.080
Okay, now we have our date August 20th, 2025.

00:16.120 --> 00:21.320
One of the things that we can do with the dates is we can go and extract different parts of the date.

00:21.360 --> 00:26.040
For example, we are interested only on the year so we can go and extract only the year part.

00:26.080 --> 00:29.920
Or if we are interested in the month, you can go and extract the month and you will go to August.

00:29.920 --> 00:33.320
And of course we can go and extract the day and we will get that 20.

00:33.360 --> 00:34.960
So this is the first thing that we can do.

00:34.960 --> 00:37.120
We can extract the parts of the dates.

00:37.160 --> 00:41.400
Now another thing that we can do is we can go and change the date format.

00:41.440 --> 00:47.680
So instead of having like a small minus between those date parts, we can go and split them using slash.

00:47.680 --> 00:52.760
We can even start first with the month August, then 20 that day, and then the year.

00:52.760 --> 00:55.400
But having only the short form of the year 25.

00:55.440 --> 00:59.720
Or we can go and change the format where we say we don't need any special character, we just leave

00:59.720 --> 01:00.720
it as a space.

01:00.720 --> 01:04.240
So as you can see, we are changing and manipulating the format of the dates.

01:04.280 --> 01:05.720
Another category or task.

01:05.720 --> 01:12.080
We can go and do date calculations, so we can go and take our date and add to it, for example three

01:12.080 --> 01:12.480
years.

01:12.520 --> 01:17.560
Or we can go and find the differences between two dates, like we are doing a subtraction or let's say

01:17.600 --> 01:20.460
a minus, and we will get for example, 30 days.

01:20.460 --> 01:24.460
So we can go and add stuff, subtract stuff, or find differences between two dates.

01:24.460 --> 01:26.500
It's like we are doing calculations on the dates.

01:26.540 --> 01:32.180
Now to the last thing that we can do with this date is we can go and test this date or validate it,

01:32.220 --> 01:35.380
whether it is a real date that SQL understands.

01:35.380 --> 01:37.780
So we can put it on the test and add the output.

01:37.820 --> 01:40.500
We're going to get true or false or zero and one.

01:40.500 --> 01:45.740
So as you can see here we have different ways or let's say categories on how to manipulate our dates

01:45.740 --> 01:46.500
in SQL.

01:46.540 --> 01:51.500
Now we're going to go and group up the different date and time functions under four categories.

01:51.500 --> 01:53.500
The first category and the most important one.

01:53.500 --> 01:55.220
We have the part extraction.

01:55.220 --> 02:00.020
And here we have around seven different functions that we can use in order to do this task.

02:00.060 --> 02:02.980
Another category we have the format and casting.

02:02.980 --> 02:04.660
And here we have three different functions.

02:04.660 --> 02:08.540
Underneath this category we have the format convert and cast.

02:08.540 --> 02:11.580
And then the third category we have the calculations of the dates.

02:11.580 --> 02:14.260
We have two functions date add and date diff.

02:14.300 --> 02:18.860
And the last category the validation we have here only one function called is dates.

02:18.860 --> 02:21.140
So as you can see we have a lot of SQL functions.

02:21.140 --> 02:25.340
We have 13 date and time functions that we're going to cover in this tutorial.

02:25.340 --> 02:28.540
And how to manipulate the date and time informations in SQL.

02:28.540 --> 02:31.660
And this is how we can group them into four different categories.

02:31.700 --> 02:33.500
Let's start now with the biggest category.

02:33.500 --> 02:35.220
We have the part extraction.

02:35.220 --> 02:39.100
We're going to cover all those seven functions in details on how to extract parts.
